• 3/21/2026
Canary [
	• Been using Canary for several months. About 60 wpm for ordinary work and overall feels very comfortable and natural.
	• However never been happy about the W on left pinky. 'W' is more common than 'C' in my writing and my pinky never feels very accurate. it it usually accurate and fast enough, just does not feel good to use so keeps me from focusing as well on work.
	• Tried remapping the character around to no good result. Tried using on left thumb key which actually feels really good except thats what I use for shift, so then have to retrain that which means also retraining backspace since I use that on right thumb. So cascading effects.
]
Gallium [
	• Tried Gallium, got up to 30wpm in about three days practice. It does spread load out better among fingers but just always feels clunky to me. Never flows. I only type the most common English characters but none of them just roll as they do in Canary. Often times they seem a bit puzzle like, having wide range of up and down, with lots of pinky and ring finger involved. Since my pinkies never feel confident I don't see this ever really clicking with me.
]
On the switch [
	• It is hard change because the home row shares a lot of keys that are just one apart, and these are the highest frequency ones. Not recommended.
	• Going back to Colemak might be better idea if anything, since it has better home row and very similar, with better 'W' key position, but been so long since I used it I forgot what made me change to Canary, may have just been curiosity. Since Colemak and Canary so similar I might take couple days to feel it out again at some point.
	 
]